<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111520" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλοσώμᾰτ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>loving the body, indulging
				it,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ φιλόσοφος, ἀλλά τις φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					68c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.16
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				158
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Demoph.
				<u>Sent.</u>
				44
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Antr.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			; distd. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλήδονος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.140c
			</span></i> (but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλήδονοι καὶ φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.Chr.
					4.115
				</span></i>
			): <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλοσωματία</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.593d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				18.1
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					3.137
				</span></i>
			.</div>
